The combined `__init__.py` compiles cleanly, all `__all__` entries resolve to defined functions/classes, and cross-function calls (e.g. `bkfe` calling `linbin`, `dpill` calling `rlbin`/`cpblock`/`blkest`/`locpoly`/`sdiag`/`sstdiag`) now resolve as plain intra-module calls since everything lives in one namespace.

Summary of what I did:
- Combined all 15 JSON-defined functions from `ablation/conversion_guides/no_guides/7/all.R/` into `r2py_kernsmooth/__init__.py`.
- Deduplicated and sorted imports into stdlib (`math`, `warnings`, `typing`) → third-party (`numpy`, `scipy.stats`) → local (`from . import _KernSmooth`) groups.
- Dropped self-referential local imports (`from .linbin import linbin`, `from .bkfe import bkfe`, `from .rlbin import rlbin`, `from .cpblock import cpblock`, `from .blkest import blkest`, `from .locpoly import locpoly`, `from .sdiag import sdiag`, `from .sstdiag import sstdiag`, `from .linbin2D import linbin2D`) — these referenced sibling modules that don't exist as separate files anymore since everything now lives in one `__init__.py`; keeping them would have caused circular self-imports.
- Verified `from . import _KernSmooth` matches the actual meson build (extension module named `_KernSmooth`, installed under `r2py_kernsmooth`), so no binding path correction was needed.
- Preserved the existing `__all__` list (14 public functions) unchanged; added `onAttach`/`_on_unload` (R package lifecycle hooks) as private-ish helpers not exported in `__all__`, consistent with the prior scaffold.
- Confirmed the file parses, compiles, and all `__all__` names resolve. Actually importing it requires the compiled `_KernSmooth` extension (meson build), which isn't built in this environment — that's expected and unrelated to the merge itself.
